## S4: Diurnal Rhythm Check

*Rationale.* An AUCi decrease could reflect either a task-related suppression or ordinary diurnal decline over the session, since steroid hormones (cortisol, DHEA, testosterone) follow a circadian rhythm that immune markers do not share. Hours since waking, not session clock time, is the more appropriate basis for this check, since the circadian decline is anchored to each person's own wake time rather than the shared clock; session start time is examined alongside it as a secondary, less-missing-data cross-check. This matches the primary notebook's Diurnal Rhythm Check exactly, re-pointed at this notebook's own `auci_data` (S3 above) and its own pre-existing `wake_time`/`hours_since_wake` (built in the setup chunk for the covariate-adjusted trend models above) and `saliva_timing$t1i_min`.




```{r s4-diurnal-check}
auci_diurnal_data <- auci_data |>
  left_join(saliva_timing |> select(SampleID, t1i_min), by = "SampleID") |>
  left_join(wake_time |> select(SampleID, hours_since_wake), by = "SampleID")

auci_diurnal_vars <- c(
  cort_auci = "Cortisol", dhea_auci = "DHEA", test_auci = "Testosterone",
  crp_auci = "CRP", il6_auci = "IL-6", il10_auci = "IL-10", tnfa_auci = "TNF-alpha"
)

cor_or_na <- function(x, y) {
  dat <- na.omit(data.frame(x, y))
  if (nrow(dat) < 3) return(list(n = nrow(dat), r = NA_real_, p = NA_real_))
  ct <- cor.test(dat$x, dat$y)
  list(n = nrow(dat), r = round(unname(ct$estimate), 3), p = round(ct$p.value, 4))
}

auci_diurnal_tbl <- imap_dfr(auci_diurnal_vars, function(label, col) {
  wake_res  <- cor_or_na(auci_diurnal_data$hours_since_wake, auci_diurnal_data[[col]])
  clock_res <- cor_or_na(auci_diurnal_data$t1i_min,          auci_diurnal_data[[col]])
  tibble(
    Biomarker = label,
    Group     = if_else(label %in% c("Cortisol", "DHEA", "Testosterone"),
                         "Hormones (circadian rhythm)", "Immune (no circadian rhythm)"),
    n_wake    = wake_res$n,  r_wake  = wake_res$r,  p_wake  = wake_res$p,
    n_clock   = clock_res$n, r_clock = clock_res$r, p_clock = clock_res$p
  )
}, .id = "var") |>
  select(-var)

fmt_time_range <- function(x) {
  x <- x[!is.na(x)]
  paste0(
    sprintf("N = %d; mean %02d:%02d; range %02d:%02d",
            length(x),
            floor(mean(x) / 60), round(mean(x) %% 60),
            floor(min(x) / 60),  round(min(x) %% 60)),
    "-",
    sprintf("%02d:%02d", floor(max(x) / 60), round(max(x) %% 60))
  )
}
session_start_summary <- fmt_time_range(auci_diurnal_data$t1i_min)
hours_wake_valid <- auci_diurnal_data$hours_since_wake[!is.na(auci_diurnal_data$hours_since_wake)]
hours_wake_summary <- paste0(
  sprintf("N = %d; mean %.1fh; range %.1f", length(hours_wake_valid), mean(hours_wake_valid), min(hours_wake_valid)),
  "-",
  sprintf("%.1fh", max(hours_wake_valid))
)

auci_diurnal_tbl |>
  mutate(
    p_wake  = cell_spec(p_wake,  bold = p_wake  < 0.05, color = if_else(p_wake  < 0.05, "#2166ac", "black")),
    p_clock = cell_spec(p_clock, bold = p_clock < 0.05, color = if_else(p_clock < 0.05, "#2166ac", "black"))
  ) |>
  kable(col.names = c("Biomarker", "Group", "n (wake)", "r (wake)", "p (wake)",
                       "n (clock)", "r (clock)", "p (clock)"),
        escape = FALSE,
        caption = paste0("Correlation between AUCi and (a) hours since waking, (b) session start time, by biomarker. Hours since waking: ",
                          hours_wake_summary, ". Session start time: ", session_start_summary, ".")) |>
  kable_styling(bootstrap_options = "hover")
```

```{r s4-diurnal-results-vals, echo=FALSE, include=FALSE}
sig_diurnal_wake_hormones <- auci_diurnal_tbl |>
  filter(Group == "Hormones (circadian rhythm)", p_wake < 0.05) |> pull(Biomarker)
sig_diurnal_wake_immune <- auci_diurnal_tbl |>
  filter(Group == "Immune (no circadian rhythm)", p_wake < 0.05) |> pull(Biomarker)
sig_diurnal_clock_hormones <- auci_diurnal_tbl |>
  filter(Group == "Hormones (circadian rhythm)", p_clock < 0.05) |> pull(Biomarker)
```




**Results.** Hours since waking (`r hours_wake_summary`) was significantly correlated with AUCi for `r fmt_or_none(sig_diurnal_wake_hormones)` — of the three steroid hormones with a known circadian rhythm — with more time since waking associated with more negative AUCi. `r if (length(sig_diurnal_wake_immune) == 0) "No immune marker" else fmt_or_none(sig_diurnal_wake_immune)` showed this relationship. Session start time (`r session_start_summary`) showed the same pattern for `r fmt_or_none(sig_diurnal_clock_hormones)`. This is consistent with normal diurnal decline contributing to the cortisol AUCi decrease reported in S3, rather than a task-specific suppression effect, matching the primary notebook's Diurnal Rhythm Check conclusion.

*Note on scope.* This check is correlation-only, matching the primary notebook. A covariate-adjusted version — testing the AUCi one-sample intercepts (S3 above) in a regression model that includes hours-since-waking as a covariate, rather than as a separate bivariate correlation — has not been implemented in either notebook; it would be new computation beyond re-narrating existing analyses, and is noted here rather than silently added.

## S5: Peak-Timepoint Sensitivity (T2-Eligible)

*Rationale.* The primary peak-vs-T1 reactivity test defines each biomarker's "peak" as the higher of T3 or T4. But a substantial share of participants -- for both immune markers and hormones -- actually peak at T2, not T3/T4 (see the table below). Timing is part of the reason: DHEA is expected to rise quickly, plausibly within T2's window (~10 min after task onset), while cortisol's slower rise (~15-20 min post-onset) means neither T2 nor T3 (~30 min) is a clean match to its expected peak -- T2 likely undershoots it and T3 may already be past it. Restricting peak-eligibility to T3/T4 therefore risks missing the true peak in either direction, and several cytokines show the same T2-heavy pattern empirically for reasons unrelated to any specific hormone-timing hypothesis (see `sos-bioreactivity-reactivity-revised.qmd`, which uses each participant's own extreme value across all four timepoints, in the *decrease* direction for hormones -- a different hypothesis than tested here). This check re-defines each biomarker's peak as the higher of T2, T3, or T4 (T1 remains excluded from the candidate set, so the test stays directly comparable in structure to the primary peak-vs-T1 test, and the direction stays an *increase* for every biomarker, matching the primary hypothesis -- only the candidate window changes) and re-runs the paired t-test against T1, for all 7 biomarkers. Whatever the theoretical timing argument, the table below reports how often each biomarker's own maximum empirically falls at T2 versus T3/T4, which is the more direct evidence for whether this candidate-set choice matters.




```{r s5-t2-setup, echo=FALSE}
peak_time_among <- function(...) {
  vals <- list(...)
  labels <- c("T2", "T3", "T4")
  purrr::pmap_chr(vals, function(...) {
    x <- c(...)
    if (all(is.na(x))) return(NA_character_)
    labels[which.max(x)]
  })
}

sos_crp_wide <- sos_crp_wide |>
  mutate(
    crp_peak_t2eligible = na_if(pmax(CRP_log_2, CRP_log_3, CRP_log_4, na.rm = TRUE), -Inf),
    crp_peak_time        = peak_time_among(CRP_log_2, CRP_log_3, CRP_log_4)
  )

sos_cytokines_wide <- sos_cytokines_wide |>
  mutate(
    il10_peak_t2eligible = na_if(pmax(IL10_log_2, IL10_log_3, IL10_log_4, na.rm = TRUE), -Inf),
    il6_peak_t2eligible  = na_if(pmax(IL6_log_2, IL6_log_3, IL6_log_4, na.rm = TRUE), -Inf),
    tnfa_peak_t2eligible = na_if(pmax(TNFalpha_log_2, TNFalpha_log_3, TNFalpha_log_4, na.rm = TRUE), -Inf),
    il10_peak_time        = peak_time_among(IL10_log_2, IL10_log_3, IL10_log_4),
    il6_peak_time         = peak_time_among(IL6_log_2, IL6_log_3, IL6_log_4),
    tnfa_peak_time        = peak_time_among(TNFalpha_log_2, TNFalpha_log_3, TNFalpha_log_4)
  )

sos_hormones_wide <- sos_hormones_wide |>
  mutate(
    dhea_peak_t2eligible = na_if(pmax(DHEA_log_2, DHEA_log_3, DHEA_log_4, na.rm = TRUE), -Inf),
    test_peak_t2eligible = na_if(pmax(Testosterone_log_2, Testosterone_log_3, Testosterone_log_4, na.rm = TRUE), -Inf),
    cort_peak_t2eligible = na_if(pmax(Cortisol_log_2, Cortisol_log_3, Cortisol_log_4, na.rm = TRUE), -Inf),
    dhea_peak_time        = peak_time_among(DHEA_log_2, DHEA_log_3, DHEA_log_4),
    test_peak_time        = peak_time_among(Testosterone_log_2, Testosterone_log_3, Testosterone_log_4),
    cort_peak_time        = peak_time_among(Cortisol_log_2, Cortisol_log_3, Cortisol_log_4)
  )

# run_peak_test()/peak_tests_raw/peak_pfdr for the primary (T3/T4-only)
# version are already defined and computed above (peak-differences chunk);
# reused here rather than recomputed. FDR split by domain (immune 1:4,
# hormones 5:7), matching that same primary convention.
t2elig_tests_raw <- list(
  crp  = run_peak_test("crp_peak_t2eligible",  "CRP_log_1",          sos_crp_wide),
  il10 = run_peak_test("il10_peak_t2eligible", "IL10_log_1",         sos_cytokines_wide),
  il6  = run_peak_test("il6_peak_t2eligible",  "IL6_log_1",          sos_cytokines_wide),
  tnfa = run_peak_test("tnfa_peak_t2eligible", "TNFalpha_log_1",     sos_cytokines_wide),
  dhea = run_peak_test("dhea_peak_t2eligible", "DHEA_log_1",         sos_hormones_wide),
  test = run_peak_test("test_peak_t2eligible", "Testosterone_log_1", sos_hormones_wide),
  cort = run_peak_test("cort_peak_t2eligible", "Cortisol_log_1",     sos_hormones_wide)
)
t2elig_praw <- map_dbl(t2elig_tests_raw, \(t) t$p.value)
t2elig_pfdr <- setNames(
  c(p.adjust(t2elig_praw[1:4], method = "fdr"), p.adjust(t2elig_praw[5:7], method = "fdr")),
  names(t2elig_praw)
)

# T2-eligible counterpart to reactivity_vars/all_difference (same convention
# as reactivity_vars_auci/all_difference_auci in S3): HR and
# subjective-stress columns unchanged; only the 7 biomarker columns swapped
# for their T2-eligible-peak equivalents.
reactivity_vars_t2peak <- c(
  "task_rs_hr_diff", "conn_dis_hr_diff", "conn_other_hr_diff", "conn_rest_hr_diff",
  "crp_t2diff", "il10_t2diff", "il6_t2diff", "tnfa_t2diff",
  "dhea_t2diff", "test_t2diff", "cort_t2diff",
  "subj_scsd_difference", "subj_scother_difference"
)

t2peak_diff_data <- sos_crp_wide |>
  transmute(SampleID, crp_t2diff = crp_peak_t2eligible - CRP_log_1) |>
  full_join(
    sos_cytokines_wide |> transmute(SampleID,
      il10_t2diff = il10_peak_t2eligible - IL10_log_1,
      il6_t2diff  = il6_peak_t2eligible  - IL6_log_1,
      tnfa_t2diff = tnfa_peak_t2eligible - TNFalpha_log_1),
    by = "SampleID"
  ) |>
  full_join(
    sos_hormones_wide |> transmute(SampleID,
      dhea_t2diff = dhea_peak_t2eligible - DHEA_log_1,
      test_t2diff = test_peak_t2eligible - Testosterone_log_1,
      cort_t2diff = cort_peak_t2eligible - Cortisol_log_1),
    by = "SampleID"
  )

all_difference_t2peak <- all_difference |>
  select(SampleID, task_rs_hr_diff, conn_dis_hr_diff, conn_other_hr_diff, conn_rest_hr_diff,
         subj_scsd_difference, subj_scother_difference) |>
  left_join(t2peak_diff_data, by = "SampleID")
```




### Which Timepoint Captured Each Biomarker's Own Maximum (T2-T4)




```{r s5-peak-timepoint}
peak_time_specs <- list(
  CRP          = sos_crp_wide$crp_peak_time,
  `IL-10`      = sos_cytokines_wide$il10_peak_time,
  `IL-6`       = sos_cytokines_wide$il6_peak_time,
  `TNF-alpha`  = sos_cytokines_wide$tnfa_peak_time,
  DHEA         = sos_hormones_wide$dhea_peak_time,
  Testosterone = sos_hormones_wide$test_peak_time,
  Cortisol     = sos_hormones_wide$cort_peak_time
)

peak_time_tbl <- imap_dfr(peak_time_specs, function(time_vec, name) {
  tibble(
    biomarker = name,
    n_T2 = sum(time_vec == "T2", na.rm = TRUE),
    n_T3 = sum(time_vec == "T3", na.rm = TRUE),
    n_T4 = sum(time_vec == "T4", na.rm = TRUE),
    n_valid = n_T2 + n_T3 + n_T4
  )
}) |>
  select(biomarker, n_valid, n_T2, n_T3, n_T4)

peak_time_tbl |>
  kable(col.names = c("Biomarker", "N (valid T2-T4)", "Peaked at T2", "Peaked at T3", "Peaked at T4"),
        caption = "Which timepoint (T2, T3, or T4) held each biomarker's own maximum") |>
  kable_styling(bootstrap_options = "hover", full_width = FALSE)
```




### Primary vs. T2-Eligible Peak-vs-T1 Test




```{r s5-t2-compare}
peak_t2_compare <- tibble(
  biomarker = c("CRP", "IL-10", "IL-6", "TNF-alpha", "DHEA", "Testosterone", "Cortisol"),
  key       = c("crp", "il10", "il6", "tnfa", "dhea", "test", "cort")
) |>
  rowwise() |>
  mutate(
    estimate_primary = round(unname(peak_tests_raw[[key]]$estimate), 3),
    t_primary         = round(unname(peak_tests_raw[[key]]$statistic), 3),
    df_primary        = round(unname(peak_tests_raw[[key]]$parameter), 1),
    p_fdr_primary     = round(unname(peak_pfdr[key]), 4),
    estimate_t2       = round(unname(t2elig_tests_raw[[key]]$estimate), 3),
    t_t2              = round(unname(t2elig_tests_raw[[key]]$statistic), 3),
    df_t2             = round(unname(t2elig_tests_raw[[key]]$parameter), 1),
    p_fdr_t2          = round(unname(t2elig_pfdr[key]), 4)
  ) |>
  ungroup() |>
  select(-key)

peak_t2_compare |>
  mutate(across(c(p_fdr_primary, p_fdr_t2), \(x) cell_spec(
    x, bold = !is.na(x) & x < 0.05, color = if_else(!is.na(x) & x < 0.05, "#2166ac", "black")
  ))) |>
  select(biomarker, estimate_primary, t_primary, df_primary, p_fdr_primary,
         estimate_t2, t_t2, df_t2, p_fdr_t2) |>
  kable(escape = FALSE,
        col.names = c("Biomarker", "Mean diff (primary)", "t (primary)", "df (primary)", "p_FDR (primary)",
                      "Mean diff (T2-eligible)", "t (T2-eligible)", "df (T2-eligible)", "p_FDR (T2-eligible)"),
        caption = "Peak vs. T1: primary (T3/T4-eligible) vs. T2-eligible peak definition, all 7 biomarkers (FDR within immune/hormones; bold = p_FDR < .05)") |>
  kable_styling(bootstrap_options = "hover", full_width = FALSE)
```

```{r s5-t2-results-vals, echo=FALSE, include=FALSE}
all_peak_keys <- c("crp", "il10", "il6", "tnfa", "dhea", "test", "cort")
sig_peak_primary <- names(peak_pfdr)[peak_pfdr < 0.05]
sig_peak_t2       <- names(t2elig_pfdr)[t2elig_pfdr < 0.05]
key_to_label <- c(crp = "CRP", il10 = "IL-10", il6 = "IL-6", tnfa = "TNF-alpha",
                   dhea = "DHEA", test = "Testosterone", cort = "Cortisol")
sig_peak_primary_label <- if (length(sig_peak_primary) == 0) "none" else paste(unname(key_to_label[sig_peak_primary]), collapse = ", ")
sig_peak_t2_label      <- if (length(sig_peak_t2) == 0) "none" else paste(unname(key_to_label[sig_peak_t2]), collapse = ", ")

# "Peak-timepoint-dependent": conclusion differs between the primary and
# T2-eligible peak definitions -- computed from the actual sets each render.
peak_t2_index_dependent <- all_peak_keys[
  (all_peak_keys %in% sig_peak_primary) != (all_peak_keys %in% sig_peak_t2)
]
peak_t2_index_dependent_label <- if (length(peak_t2_index_dependent) == 0) NULL else
  paste(unname(key_to_label[peak_t2_index_dependent]), collapse = ", ")
```




**Results.** Under the primary (T3/T4-eligible) peak definition, `r sig_peak_primary_label` showed significant peak-vs-T1 reactivity (FDR-corrected within immune markers and hormones separately). Under the T2-eligible peak definition, `r sig_peak_t2_label` did. `r if (!is.null(peak_t2_index_dependent_label)) paste0("The conclusion for ", peak_t2_index_dependent_label, " changes depending on whether T2 is an eligible peak candidate -- this result should be considered sensitive to that modeling choice.") else "No biomarker's significance conclusion changed between the two peak definitions."` The table above (Which Timepoint Captured Each Biomarker's Own Maximum) reports how often each biomarker's own maximum actually falls at T2 versus T3/T4, which contextualizes how much this candidate-set choice matters empirically for this sample.

### Pubertal Status & Timing × Reactivity: Peak vs. T2-Eligible Peak




```{r s5-puberty-t2-compare, echo=FALSE}
timing_reactivity_t2peak <- all_difference_t2peak |>
  left_join(timing_df, by = "SampleID")

all_pub_mat_t2peak <- timing_reactivity_t2peak |>
  select(all_of(c(all_pub_vars, reactivity_vars_t2peak))) |>
  as.matrix()
colnames(all_pub_mat_t2peak) <- c(all_pub_labels, reactivity_labels)

all_pub_corrs_t2peak <- rcorr(all_pub_mat_t2peak)

raw_allpub_mat_t2peak <- all_pub_corrs_t2peak$P[all_pub_labels, reactivity_labels, drop = FALSE]
fdr_allpub_mat_t2peak <- raw_allpub_mat_t2peak
for (pv in all_pub_labels) {
  for (cols in list(hr_cols, imm_cols, horm_cols, subj_cols)) {
    fdr_allpub_mat_t2peak[pv, cols] <- p.adjust(raw_allpub_mat_t2peak[pv, cols], method = "fdr")
  }
}
r_mat_t2peak <- all_pub_corrs_t2peak$r[all_pub_labels, reactivity_labels, drop = FALSE]

# r_mat/fdr_allpub_mat (primary, peak-based) already computed in S3
# (s3-puberty-peak-corr chunk); reused here rather than recomputed.
peak_vs_t2_pub <- expand.grid(pv = all_pub_labels, rv = reactivity_labels[5:11],
                               stringsAsFactors = FALSE) |>
  rowwise() |>
  mutate(
    r_peak     = round(r_mat[pv, rv], 3),
    p_fdr_peak = round(fdr_allpub_mat[pv, rv], 4),
    r_t2       = round(r_mat_t2peak[pv, rv], 3),
    p_fdr_t2   = round(fdr_allpub_mat_t2peak[pv, rv], 4)
  ) |>
  ungroup()

peak_vs_t2_pub |>
  mutate(across(c(p_fdr_peak, p_fdr_t2), \(x) cell_spec(
    x, bold = !is.na(x) & x < 0.05, color = if_else(!is.na(x) & x < 0.05, "#2166ac", "black")
  ))) |>
  kable(escape = FALSE,
        col.names = c("Predictor", "Reactivity outcome", "r (T3/T4 peak)", "p_FDR (T3/T4 peak)",
                      "r (T2-eligible peak)", "p_FDR (T2-eligible peak)"),
        caption = "Pubertal status/timing x biomarker reactivity: T3/T4-eligible vs. T2-eligible peak definition (bold = p_FDR < .05)") |>
  kable_styling(bootstrap_options = "hover")
```

```{r s5-puberty-t2-index-dependent, echo=FALSE, include=FALSE}
pub_t2_index_dependent <- peak_vs_t2_pub |>
  filter(p_fdr_peak < 0.05, is.na(p_fdr_t2) | p_fdr_t2 >= 0.05)
pub_t2_index_dependent_text <- if (nrow(pub_t2_index_dependent) == 0) NULL else
  paste(paste0(pub_t2_index_dependent$pv, " × ", pub_t2_index_dependent$rv), collapse = ", ")
```




**Results.** Full head-to-head values for all pubertal-status/timing × biomarker-reactivity pairs, under the T3/T4-eligible vs. T2-eligible peak definitions, are shown above. `r if (!is.null(pub_t2_index_dependent_text)) paste0("The association", if (nrow(pub_t2_index_dependent) != 1) "s" else "", " between ", pub_t2_index_dependent_text, " should be considered peak-timepoint-dependent: significant under the T3/T4-eligible peak definition but not under the T2-eligible one.") else "No pair that was significant under the T3/T4-eligible peak definition lost significance under the T2-eligible one."`

